{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"privy-accurate-perch","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# S4 — Best-effort OpenAI-compatible endpoint: honor REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL, retire the loud refusal\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:653` (`_pai_check_config`) raises on any `base_url`/`api_key`, while\n`docs/llm-framework.md:126-133,226` documents both as working and shows an LMStudio/Ollama recipe, and\n`src/rebar/llm/config.py:502-503,611-612` already parses them. The documentation is false today. The refusal was\na deliberate placeholder: commit `75e598a41` describes it as \"a loud guard that REFUSES base_url/api_key rather\nthan silently dropping them (a capability gap vs langgraph, surfaced not hidden)\". This story fills the\nplaceholder it was created for.\n\n## Approach\n\nRegister an `openai` builder in the provider factory [rebar:7468-25e5-ae4f-43d1] that constructs\n`OpenAIChatModel` with `OpenAIProvider(base_url=cfg.base_url, api_key=…)`, gated behind the opt-in\n`pydantic-ai-slim[openai]` extra with a clear missing-extra error. Crucially, `base_url` is provider\n**configuration**, not provider **selection**: the provider still comes from the model string /\n`REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER`, exactly as `docs/llm-framework.md:132` already documents\n(`REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL=…`). Capability handling comes free from S2\n[rebar:f184-a5f1-f181-4700] — an opaque endpoint resolves to the conservative record, so structured output takes\nthe prompted path without any per-call boolean.\n\n`_pai_check_config` stops refusing and instead validates: an absolute-URL check on `base_url`, and an\n`api_key`-without-`base_url` error (ambiguous, since the direct OpenAI path reads `OPENAI_API_KEY`). For a\nno-auth local server an explicit placeholder key is sent so construction succeeds; a hosted endpoint answers\nwith its own 401.\n\nThis story also **documents the accidental capability** found during design: a non-loopback `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`\nalready routes rebar through an Anthropic-wire gateway, because `anthropic_model.py:60`\n(`_local_proxy_bypass_base_url`) only overrides loopback hosts and the SDK reads the env var. It works today by\naccident; this story makes it deliberate and tested.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** branching on `cfg.base_url` before provider inference (PR #121's shape). That makes\n`base_url` silently override an explicit `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER`, contradicting rebar's own documented\nrecipe, and adds a fourth implicit provider selector alongside the model string, the provider env var, and\n`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/providers.py` — the `openai` builder.\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — `_pai_check_config` (`:653`) becomes validation.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — composition semantics for `base_url` + `model_provider`.\n- `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py` — replace `test_unsupported_config_is_a_loud_error`.\n- `tests/unit/test_openai_compatible_provider.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\nContract tier: the defect class is a consumer (the runner) reading configuration the wrong way, so the test must\nrun through real config resolution rather than calling the builder directly.\n\n- happy path: `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai` + `REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1` yields an\n  `OpenAIChatModel` whose provider carries that exact base URL and the configured api_key.\n- contrast case (the PR #121 regression this exists to prevent): `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic` +\n  `REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL=…` still resolves the **anthropic** provider — base_url must not hijack selection.\n- failure paths: `api_key` without `base_url` raises `LLMConfigError`; a non-absolute `base_url` raises naming\n  the variable; a missing `openai` extra raises naming the install command.\n- edge: no api_key + a local base_url constructs successfully with the placeholder key.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the exact recipe printed at `docs/llm-framework.md:131-133` runs end-to-end against a local\n      OpenAI-compatible server (or a stub server in-test) and returns a valid structured verdict\n- [ ] a test asserts `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic` + `REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL` resolves the anthropic provider\n- [ ] `_pai_check_config` no longer raises for a valid `base_url`, and its three validation errors each have a test\n- [ ] a test pins the `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` non-loopback gateway behavior so it can no longer change by accident","id":"dc0d-886a-519c-4bf7","parent_id":"061c-ecd1-8967-4a76","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S4 — best-effort OpenAI-compatible endpoint: honor REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL, retire the loud refusal"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785008497378205001,"uuid":"0b82c7bb-fa79-45b3-b6ce-46a3fb7ad349"}